===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A thing or a person put in the [[rear]] or in the [[back]] of something to [[reinforce]], [[hold]], [[support]].
#: ''“A '''backstop''' that would be strictly time-limited would defeat the purpose of a '''backstop'''.”'' The Express 7 June 2018
#: ''Irish prime minister Leo Varadkar, this morning, said a time-limited '''backstop''' would be unacceptable, and has previously promised to vote down the UK’s Brexit withdrawal deal unless it features a satisfactory '''backstop'''.'' The Express 7 June 2018
# {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[wall]] or [[fence]] behind [[home plate]].
# {{lb|en|baseball|_|slang}} A catcher; the position of catcher.
# {{lb|en|rounders}} The player who stands immediately behind the striking base.
# {{lb|en|cricket|dated}} The [[longstop]].
# {{lb|en|cricket|dated}} The [[wicket-keeper]].

